.TH AETHERSDR "1" "2026-11-08" "AetherSDR" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
AetherSDR \- software-defined radio transceiver client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aethersdr
.RB [ --debug-level
.IR level ]
.RB [ --no-splash ]
.br
.B aethersdr
.RB [ -h | --help ]
.br
.B aethersdr --config
.I command
.RI [ key ] " " [ value ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AetherSDR is a native Qt6 and C++20 client for software-defined radios. It
speaks the SmartSDR protocol to FlexRadio transceivers, and also runs the
Hermes-Lite 2, HackRF and RTL-SDR.
.PP
This build is W5TSU's fork, maintained mainly for Hermes-Lite 2 support. It is
not an official AetherSDR release.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.BI --debug-level " level\fR, " --debug-level= level
How much of the log to print on the terminal (stderr). Each level adds to the
one before it:
.RS
.TP
.B 0
Nothing. This is the default.
.TP
.B 1
Info.
.TP
.B 2
Info, warnings and errors.
.TP
.B 3
All of the above, plus debug. Debug lines appear only for the categories
enabled in \fBHelp \(-> Support\fR.
.RE
.IP
The level doesn't change the log file in \fB~/.config/AetherSDR/logs/\fR. Libraries AetherSDR loads may still print their own messages. Any other
value prints a usage message and exits with status 1.
.TP
.B --no-splash
Skip the startup splash screen. It is also skipped when \fBAETHER_AUTOMATION\fR
is set or the Qt platform is \fBoffscreen\fR.
.TP
.BI --config " command"
Inspect or change settings without starting the GUI, then exit. Must be the
first argument. See \fBCONFIG COMMANDS\fR.
.PP
Standard Qt options, such as \fB-platform\fR and \fB-style\fR, also apply.
.SH CONFIG COMMANDS
Settings live in a SQLite store under the user config directory
(\fB~/.config/AetherSDR/AetherSDR.db\fR). The \fB--config\fR mode
inspects or repairs them without starting the GUI and then exits:
.TP
.B list \fR[\fIprefix\fR]
Print every setting as key<TAB>value, optionally filtered by key prefix.
.TP
.B get \fIkey\fR
Print one value (exit status 2 if the key does not exist).
.TP
.B set \fIkey\fR \fIvalue\fR
Create or change a setting, verifying it persisted.
.TP
.B unset \fIkey\fR
Delete a setting.
.TP
.B export
Sanitized dump of the whole store (secrets redacted); diagnostic output,
not a restorable backup.
.TP
.B features \fR[\fIfamily\fR]
List the settings stored per radio, such as Hermes-Lite 2 state, nicknames
and band stacks (sanitized).
.TP
.B path
Print the settings database path.
.PP
A running AetherSDR doesn't see changes made this way until it is restarted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/AetherSDR/AetherSDR.db
Settings.
.TP
.B ~/.config/AetherSDR/logs/aethersdr.log
The current log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
This fork: https://github.com/W5TSU/AetherSDR
.br
Official project: https://github.com/aethersdr/AetherSDR
